<title>CANADA: Loewen sees Rose purchase adding to profit.</title>
<headline>Loewen sees Rose purchase adding to profit.</headline>
<dateline>BURNABY, British Columbia 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Loewen Group Inc said on Thursday it expects its purchase of the cemetery and mortuary operations and assets of Los Angeles-based Rose Hills Memorial Park Association and Roses Inc for US$240 million to add to earnings next year.</p>
<p>To date in 1996, Loewen has been involved in acquisitions or structured deals worth US$1.3 billion. It has signed or closed US$797 million in acquisitions. And with Blackstone Capital Partners II Merchant Banking Fund L.P., Loewen invested in two highly innovative structured deals worth US$535 million.</p>
</text>
